course: dictionary
lesson: 14876
title: Reassurance: words that calm us
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Reassurance is what someone gives you to stop you feeling worried or afraid. It can be kind words, like «You will be fine», or an action, like a hug. «Mum gave me a hug and some reassurance before my spelling test.» The hug and the kind words made the worry smaller.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Children often need reassurance before a test, a visit to the doctor or the first day at a new school. Ask yourself: does this make someone feel less worried? If it does, the word is reassurance.
explain: Reassurance can also be a promise that something is true or safe. «The teacher gave us reassurance that the fire alarm was only a practice.» When something online feels scary, you can ask a trusted adult for reassurance. Asking is clever, not silly.
fact: Reassurance means words or actions that make someone feel less worried or afraid.
fact: You can give reassurance, need reassurance, look for reassurance, or offer words of reassurance.
fact: «Reassurance» is usually uncountable, so you say some reassurance, not a reassurance, in most sentences.
fact: A hug or a calm, kind voice can give reassurance without any words at all.
fact: «Reassure» is the verb: it means to make someone feel less worried.
exercise: «Before the test, Sam's teacher gave him some reassurance.» What does reassurance mean here? | Ways to run faster | A loud bell for the end of lesson | *Words that made Sam feel less worried | A test with lots of questions
exercise: «Lily felt scared, so her dad gave her a hug and kind words of reassurance.» What did the hug and the words do? | Made Lily feel hungry | *Made Lily feel less worried | Made Lily run out of the room | Made the room darker
exercise: «Ben looked for reassurance before his first day at a new school.» What was Ben looking for? | A football match | A map of the town | *Words or actions that would make him feel calmer | A new school bag
test: «The nurse gave me reassurance before the injection, and I felt braver.» What is reassurance? | A kind of medicine | *Words or actions that make someone feel less afraid | A type of injection | A loud noise
test: «When a video online felt scary, Maya asked her mum for reassurance.» Who should Maya ask for reassurance? | Nobody, she should keep it secret | *A trusted adult | The video itself | A stranger she met online
exam: Which sentence shows someone giving reassurance? | «I like red apples.» | «The bus was late again.» | «The river was very wide.» | *«Don't worry, we will look after you.»
